## Exp49 — Symmetric Boundary-Proximity Timing Family — FAIL

Purpose: test the frozen symmetric corridor-boundary timing family for binary EXIT-vs-NO_EXIT using TRAIN-only discrete-time hazards with 24 elapsed-step intercepts.

Frozen candidates were:
T1 EDGE_REL=abs(2*Position-1)
T2 LOG_NEAR_ATR=log1p(min(d_back_atr,d_forward_atr))
T3 LOG_FAR_ATR=log1p(max(d_back_atr,d_forward_atr))
T4 LOG_HARMONIC_ATR=log1p(2*d_back_atr*d_forward_atr/(d_back_atr+d_forward_atr))

All exact upstream/split/eligible-cell/joint-environment guards PASS. All eight EXIT environments scorable. JOINT4 TRAIN design rank=28/28, converged=True, finite=True; EXP49_JOINT4_IDENTIFIABILITY=PASS. TRAIN feature rank=4/4; standardized condition number 19.409. LOG_NEAR_ATR and LOG_HARMONIC_ATR were strongly redundant (r=0.980036), but numerical identifiability was not the reason for failure.

Formal JOINT4_EXIT vs BASE_EXIT, EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED, whole-BRT-day bootstrap:
VAL_EARLY_UP Brier +.063545944 CI[+.038281900,+.101323113] PASS; LL +.163310290 CI[+.101588623,+.259531176] PASS.
VAL_EARLY_DOWN Brier +.039709301 CI[-.003702332,+.091116335] FAIL; LL +.088947452 CI[-.028678103,+.224686388] FAIL.
VAL_LATE_UP Brier +.069943888 CI[+.030945903,+.110518539] PASS; LL +.169355653 CI[+.074903833,+.269179699] PASS.
VAL_LATE_DOWN Brier +.077406423 CI[+.036248954,+.117334934] PASS; LL +.193371278 CI[+.101864174,+.290579422] PASS.
TEST_EARLY_UP Brier +.125532201 CI[+.067713065,+.157237046] PASS; LL +.310607627 CI[+.176528226,+.388664137] PASS.
TEST_EARLY_DOWN Brier +.092127747 CI[+.050375801,+.144155432] PASS; LL +.226397813 CI[+.119815246,+.357329989] PASS.
TEST_LATE_UP Brier +.038636157 CI[-.015737434,+.087338104] FAIL; LL +.075348633 CI[-.080261046,+.207232021] FAIL.
TEST_LATE_DOWN Brier +.036412324 CI[+.010604073,+.065416489] PASS; LL +.089388538 CI[+.024739209,+.160412214] PASS.

Formal cells passing: 12/16. Therefore:
EXP49_EXIT_ENVIRONMENT_STATUS=PASS
EXP49_JOINT4_IDENTIFIABILITY=PASS
TIMING_GEOMETRY_FAMILY=FAIL
ROBUST_SYMMETRIC_EXIT_GEOMETRY=FAIL
EXP49_FORMAL_STATUS=FAIL

Diagnostics cannot rescue this FAIL. However, all 32 environment×horizon JOINT4 point AUCs were above 0.5, approximately 0.6970–0.9826. Even the two formal loss-failure environments retained substantial discrimination: VALIDATION_EARLY__FULL_DOWN AUC ~0.7485–0.8002 and TEST_LATE__FULL_UP ~0.6970–0.8221. Their principal weakness was absolute probability level/calibration, with frequent overprediction of EXIT probability. This motivates Exp50 as a decomposition test, not a rescue.

Drop-one diagnostic: removing LOG_HARMONIC_ATR slightly improved some pooled VALIDATION/TEST losses; LOG_FAR_ATR was near-neutral; LOG_NEAR_ATR carried meaningful incremental information in several pooled comparisons. These are diagnostic facts only and do not redefine Exp49.

Exp49 failure does not erase Exp44/45/47 PASS results. Position remains robust WHICH-SIDE; calibrated universal WHEN/WHETHER remains unestablished.

## Exp50 — Exit-Risk Ranking Transport Decomposition — FROZEN BEFORE SCORE

Scientific question: does the exact original TRAIN-fitted Exp49 JOINT4_EXIT geometry model robustly rank which states are more likely to EXIT by a fixed horizon, even though Exp49 failed strict transport of absolute Brier/LogLoss probabilities?

This is a decomposition of discrimination vs calibration. It is NOT a new predictor search, NOT recalibration, and NOT a rescue of Exp49.

Frozen model/data:
- Reuse exact Exp49 JOINT4_EXIT unchanged: same TRAIN-only fit, same four frozen geometry features, same 24 elapsed-step intercepts.
- Reuse exact Exp41 eligible cells, horizons H={15,30,60,120}m, and exact eight Exp44/45 direction×time environments.
- Target y_exit=1 for ADVANCE or RECAPTURE by H; 0 for NO_EXIT by H.
- No Dwell, no signed Position timing feature, no new feature, no refit, no recalibration, no threshold.

Primary estimand:
- Ranking/discrimination within each fixed environment × fixed horizon.
- Metric: ROC AUC of p_EXIT_JOINT4 for y_exit.
- BASE_EXIT is constant across states within a fixed horizon and therefore has AUC=0.5; formal null is AUC=0.5.
- 8 environments × 4 horizons = 32 mandatory ranking cells.

Cluster inference frozen before score:
- 10,000 bootstrap replicates.
- Resample whole contributing BRT days with replacement within each environment×horizon; all rows from a selected day receive its bootstrap multiplicity.
- Compute weighted ROC AUC including 0.5 credit for tied scores.
- A bootstrap replicate is valid only when weighted EXIT and NO_EXIT totals are both positive.
- A cell is scorable only if the original cell has both classes, >=2 contributing BRT days, and >=95% (>=9500/10000) valid bootstrap replicates.
- Formal cell PASS requires 95% bootstrap CI lower bound for AUC > 0.5.

Formal gate:
- GEOMETRY_EXIT_RANKING_TRANSPORT=PASS only if all 32 mandatory environment×horizon cells are scorable and all 32 lower CI bounds exceed 0.5.
- ROBUST_EXIT_URGENCY_ORDERING=PASS only under the same 32/32 gate and exact Exp49 JOINT4 numerical-identifiability reproduction.
- EXP50_FORMAL_STATUS=PASS only under those conditions.

Diagnostics only:
- point AUC and AUC-0.5 margin;
- observed EXIT rate vs mean JOINT4 probability (calibration gap) per environment×horizon;
- descriptive AUC heterogeneity across direction/time/horizon.

Interpretation if PASS:
- establish only robust relative EXIT-risk/urgency ordering within the repeatedly inspected historical universe;
- do NOT claim universally calibrated P(EXIT by H), exact timing probability, or Exp49 reversal;
- Exp49 remains FAIL and Exp47 minimal factorized probability law remains preserved PASS.

Interpretation if FAIL:
- symmetric geometry is not universally transportable even as an EXIT-risk ranking law under this historical stress.

Anti-rescue:
- no alternate AUC definition after result;
- no pooled-horizon AUC replacing a failed horizon;
- no dropped environment/horizon;
- no side/era-specific refit;
- no recalibration/intercept/threshold;
- no alternate feature subset or transform;
- no Validation/TEST refit;
- no Exp27 scoring/modification.

Historical OOS remains exploratory because it has been repeatedly inspected. Fresh-forward Exp27 remains the decisive anti-overfitting gate before runtime promotion.
